  "details": "dear all,\ni just came across a possible idea in my head to help against heavy avatars (possibly crash ones too) to keep performance for user clients up.\nthat idea being: a automatic avatar hiding system, that one can set to some levels once their total total processing time takes too long, polled at a certain period (if enabled) per avatar in a instance or so on client side.\nthe settings can be:\navatar auto performance: on/off\navatar auto performance level: (1-10) - where the number means the max average milliseconds processing time time per avatar (of say the past second)\nthis can also can help with telemetry logging to improve user experience and possibly get rid of crashers as such:\nreporting back to the team each vrchat start to see which avatars are likely crashers (due to repeated time start but client crash without finish processing avatar)\ni hope this issue sometime gets implemented, as it might be very usefull for those with pc's meeting the minimum vrchat specifications, but not much more than that.\nif something is unclear, feel free to contact me back for any clarification! (as english is not my native language)\nyours, 8bit-bunny. (twitter: 8bit_bun)",
